WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.720
"Europe will not be made all at once,

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.800
or according to a single plan.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.640
It will be built through concrete achievements

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.280
which first create a de facto solidarity."

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.040
Solidarity has always been at the heart

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.560
of the European community. 

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.440
Seventy years ago, on May the 9th, 1950,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.160
Robert Schuman made a revolutionary declaration.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.600
With Europe ravaged by the Second World War,

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.240
Schuman planted the seed

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.680
from which the European community of peace

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.720
grew and blossomed.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.280
Former enemies reached out their hands in reconciliation

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.240
and became friends. 

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.080
We opened borders and tore down the walls between us.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.680
We built the world's biggest internal market.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.880
With the continent reunified,

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.560
the European family finally became whole again.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.040
Against all odds, we built a unique society in Europe,

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.680
where we can live together in peace and solidarity.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.360
Today, 70 years after the Schuman Declaration,

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.760
Europeans are confronted with the deepest crisis

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.120
since the Second World War.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.840
Too many have lost loved ones,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.760
are fighting for their own lives

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.200
or are afraid of losing their jobs,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.200
their livelihoods,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.440
their future.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.400
Still, in the midst of today's crisis,

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.240
the European spirit of solidarity was rekindled.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.520
Leaving borders open for critical transport

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.480
of food and medical goods,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.880
helping EU citizens travel safely home,

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.120
supporting neighbouring countries with medical staff,

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.200
investing massive resources to find a vaccine.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.280
In the midst of this crisis, new heroes have emerged.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.520
They are our inspiration.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.960
Now, we are called upon to walk in the footsteps of Schuman

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.520
to write the next chapter in our history.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.880
It is time to re-build Europe with a new recovery plan

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.200
and a heart.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.720
It is time for a Europe where workers 

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.800
have a good job to return to after the crisis,

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.440
where companies receive a helping hand,

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.080
especially in hard hit sectors.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.440
A Europe where we harvest the energy of sun, wind and water

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.000
to fuel our cars, homes and factories.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.920
A Europe where we join forces and invest in research

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.880
to give citizens the healthcare they need.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:42.760
It is time to help each other become stronger together.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.920
It's time to be brave, to stand up

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.640
and build a better future.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.960
It is time to make history again.

